  "plan": "First explore the environment to understand what's installed. Check OS, availability of git/nginx/sshd, whether a git user exists, and whether services are running. Then I'll build the solution: create git user with password auth, set up bare repo with post-receive hook, generate self-signed cert, configure nginx on 8443, and test the full push->deploy flow.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/os-release | head -5; echo '---'; which git nginx sshd ssh; echo '---'; id git 2>/dev/null || echo 'no git user'; service --status-all 2>/dev/null | head\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Environment is Ubuntu 26.04 with git, nginx, sshd all installed. No 'git' user exists yet. Nothing is running. I need to: create a git user with password auth, create a bare repo at /git/project with a post-receive hook that deploys main/dev branches to /var/www, generate a self-signed cert, configure nginx on 8443 with HTTPS, and start sshd + nginx.",
  "plan": "Run a sequence of setup commands: (1) create git user with password 'password'; (2) init bare repo /git/project; (3) install post-receive hook; (4) chown dirs; (5) generate self-signed cert; (6) write nginx config for 8443 with root /var/www/main and alias /dev -> /var/www/dev; (7) enable sshd password auth; (8) start sshd and nginx; (9) seed main and dev branches by pushing to the bare repo (triggers hook/deploy); (10) verify services listening and both URLs serve content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "useradd -m -s /bin/bash git 2>/dev/null; echo 'git:password' | chpasswd; id git\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /git /var/www/main /var/www/dev; git init --bare -b main /git/project >/dev/null; ls /git/project\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /git/project/hooks/post-receive <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\nwhile read oldrev newrev refname; do\n  [ \"$newrev\" = \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\" ] && continue\n  branch=\"${refname#refs/heads/}\"\n  case \"$branch\" in\n    main) target=/var/www/main ;;\n    dev) target=/var/www/dev ;;\n    *) continue ;;\n  esac\n  mkdir -p \"$target\"\n  find \"$target\" -mindepth 1 -delete\n  git --git-dir=/git/project archive \"$newrev\" | tar -x -C \"$target\"\ndone\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x /git/project/hooks/post-receive; chown -R git:git /git /var/www; ls -la /git/project/hooks/\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /etc/nginx/ssl; openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout /etc/nginx/ssl/nginx.key -out /etc/nginx/ssl/nginx.crt -subj \"/CN=localhost\" 2>/dev/null; ls -la /etc/nginx/ssl/\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /etc/nginx/conf.d/git.conf <<'EOF'\nserver {\n    listen 8443 ssl;\n    server_name localhost;\n    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/nginx.crt;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/nginx.key;\n    root /var/www/main;\n    index index.html;\n    location /dev {\n        alias /var/www/dev;\n    }\n}\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.3
