    {
      "keystrokes": "usermod -s /bin/bash git; getent passwd git\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "time /tmp/push_ssh.exp\n",
      "duration": 8.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- MAIN after SSH push ---'; curl -sk https://localhost:8443/index.html\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Reverting to /bin/bash didn't fix the SSH push — it still fails with 'Could not read from remote repository', which means the server-side git-receive-pack is failing before hook execution. The earlier `echo HELLO_MARKER` diagnostic also didn't print output, suggesting the command path is the problem (likely git-receive-pack not found in the sshd session PATH, or a repo access issue as the git user). I need to get the actual server-side error. I'll set up a key for clean non-interactive diagnostics and test git-receive-pack directly as the git user.",
  "plan": "1) Generate an SSH key for root and add it to git's authorized_keys (for debugging only; password auth remains enabled). 2) Run `ssh git@localhost 'git-receive-pack /git/project'` with closed stdin to capture the real error. 3) Also test `which git-receive-pack` and PATH as the git user. 4) Inspect /git/project ownership. Based on the captured error I'll apply the correct fix (likely PATH for git-receive-pack, or a safe.directory issue).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N '' -q; mkdir -p /home/git/.ssh; cat /root/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub >> /home/git/.ssh/authorized_keys; chown -R git:git /home/git/.ssh; chmod 700 /home/git/.ssh; chmod 600 /home/git/.ssh/authorized_keys; echo KEYSETUP_DONE\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh -o BatchMode=yes git@localhost 'echo PATH=$PATH; which git-receive-pack; id' 2>&1 | head\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh -o BatchMode=yes git@localhost 'git-receive-pack /git/project' </dev/null 2>&1 | head -20\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Key finding: even a plain `ssh git@localhost 'echo PATH=$PATH'` produced NO output, and `git-receive-pack /git/project` also produced nothing. So remote command execution isn't returning output at all — this is why the push fails with a generic 'Could not read from remote repository'. The shell is /bin/bash, key auth works (no password prompt), so something prevents the command's stdout from coming back. I need to capture the real cause with verbose ssh and a simple echo test.",
  "plan": "Run focused diagnostics: (1) a trivial `ssh git@localhost 'echo TEST123'` to confirm whether ANY output returns; (2) `ssh -v` to see the session negotiation; (3) check git user's shell/login shell behavior. This will reveal whether the issue is the shell, an sshd ForceCommand/Match block, or output being swallowed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh git@localhost 'echo TEST123' ; echo \"RC=$?\"\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh -v git@localhost 'echo VTEST' 2>&1 | tail -25\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Critical clue: even a trivial `ssh git@localhost 'echo TEST123'` returns exit code 254 with NO output, and `ssh -v` shows auth succeeds but the command produces no output and exits 254. This is a session-level failure, not a git problem. The most likely cause in a container is a PAM session module (e.g. pam_systemd) failing during session open, which makes sshd refuse to run the command. I'll confirm via auth.log, then disable PAM in sshd (password auth still works via sshd's built-in crypt check) and retest.",
  "plan": "1) Check auth.log for the session failure reason. 2) Set `UsePAM no` in sshd_config (this bypasses PAM session modules while PasswordAuthentication remains enabled and uses the OS shadow check). 3) Restart sshd. 4) Test a plain remote command — if it returns RC=0 with output, the session works. Then re-run the real SSH push test.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n 25 /var/log/auth.log 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/^#*UsePAM .*/UsePAM no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config; grep -qi '^UsePAM' /etc/ssh/sshd_config || echo 'UsePAM no' >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config; grep -ni usepam /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "pkill sshd; sleep 0.5; /usr/sbin/sshd; sleep 0.5; ss -tlnp 2>/dev/null | grep ':22'\n",
      "duration": 1.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ssh git@localhost 'echo RC=$?'\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

